+# Garvey’s May follow-up, January submission and interview records
+
+November 9, 2026 Eastern · B129 / PD01 / PD07. The January 27 written submission explicitly returns to the May 22 threat questions. It points to a classified statement prepared for the congressional Joint Inquiry and leaves the incidents themselves outside its coverage. The public record includes the written supplement and Garvey’s oral account of submitting it. The evidence needed to identify any enclosure or establish delivery of the classified statement remains outstanding. [January written submission](https://govinfo.library.unt.edu/911/hearings/hearing7/witness_garvey.htm) · [January transcript](https://www.9-11commission.gov/archive/hearing7/9-11Commission_Hearing_2004-01-27.htm#one)
+
+## Follow the two documents separately
+
+| Record | What the cited passage supports |
+| --- | --- |
+| May 22, 2003 transcript, saved HTML lines 3679–3698 | Garvey offers more information on the cited cases. Roemer distinguishes the domestic Langley example from Garvey’s description of an overseas focus. Garvey reiterates her offer and qualifies her account of source credibility. Preserve those accounts with their speakers. [May transcript](https://www.9-11commission.gov/archive/hearing2/9-11Commission_Hearing_2003-05-22.htm) |
+| January 27, 2004 written submission, saved HTML lines 72–76 and 100–102 | Garvey cites the May hearing, prior written testimony and a later staff meeting. She identifies the former FAA Office of Civil Aviation Security Intelligence as the preparer of a detailed classified statement for the Joint Inquiry. She hopes it answers the questions and states, “I do not specifically address the incidents here.” She gives her broader assessment that the FAA had received no intelligence supporting a specific, credible suicide-aircraft threat. [January submission](https://govinfo.library.unt.edu/911/hearings/hearing7/witness_garvey.htm) |
+| January 27 hearing transcript, saved HTML line 171 | Garvey says she submitted supplemental written testimony for the Commission record. This is a public account of submission and identifies the written testimony. A received copy, enclosure list and intake entry would establish the package contents. [January transcript](https://www.9-11commission.gov/archive/hearing7/9-11Commission_Hearing_2004-01-27.htm#one) |
+| FAA AWA-811, physical p. 1, page-text lines 14–25 | The unclassified comments also name the former intelligence office and a detailed classified Joint Inquiry response. They identify TSA as a source for the full report. The common office, recipient, subject and classification describe a candidate relationship between the references. The approved versions and custody evidence are needed to establish it. [AWA-811, p. 1](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/dc-metro/rg-237/7419198-9-11-faa/5-Miscellaneous/e-Other/5-AWA-811-Report-Threat-Info-Received-by-FAA-Before-9-11.pdf#page=1) |
+| Commission report, Chapter 10 note 14, saved HTML line 1834 | The Commission separately cites an undated FAA/TSA rebuttal, p. 1, for its discussion of the August 1998 report. This is evidence of a cited rebuttal. Its exact identity and intake route remain open. [Commission endnotes](https://www.911commission.gov/report/911Report_Notes.htm) |
+
+The public materials support an explicit subject link between the May questions and the January submission. The archived October interview could be the staff meeting cited in January. The submission gives no date for that meeting. The endnote could refer to a separately supplied rebuttal version. Compare the cited page, accession or registry number, original cover, enclosure list and receiving entry before joining the records. The May 23 read-in of the original NORAD answer and the separate correction recommended by DOT OIG in 2006 remain distinct events. [Prior May read-in analysis](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/main/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-garvey-witness-supplement-2026-11-06/README.md) · [DOT OIG recommendations, pp. 12–13](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/cc2006085.pdf#page=12)
+
+## Five archival scans
+
+- **October 21 interview, two copies.** Team 7 Box 10 and Front Office Box 3 Tab 9-18 each have 12 pages. In both copies, p. 3 lines 13–19 report that Garvey did not recall seeing a 1995 estimate, a 1998 FAA assessment and a 1999 FAA Intelligence Note, and learned more about a briefing CD-ROM after the attacks. Page 7 lines 32–33 record her relative threat assessment. Page 10 lines 17–20 records her recollection when shown several versions of the day-of-attack executive summary. Those are attributed recollections. Document distribution, content, receipt and recall are separate observations. [Exact ZIP members and locators](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+- **Copy-specific differences.** Page 1 extraction gives `Date: October 21,2003` in Team 7 and `Date: October 21, 2003` in Tab 9-18. Both images show the same calendar date. At the p. 3 paragraph opening, the Team 7 image shows a crossed-through `[SSI]` and its extracted text omits it. Tab 9-18 shows and extracts `[SSI]` without a crossing. The p. 9 foot region in Team 7 shows handwritten marginalia and a marked printed acronym. The counterpart lacks that legible note and shows `CVTS`. The extraction gives `the^VTS` in Team 7 and `the CVTS` in Tab 9-18. The markings, printed text and extraction results remain separate. Author, annotation date, circulation and copy order are unresolved. [Page render and text hashes](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+- **Hearing question and working notes.** Team 7 Box 7’s two-page member is indexed as a question for Garvey about Eberhart and planes as missiles, with the archive filename describing it as a question that was never asked. Both images contain draft language contrasting reported NORAD preparation with a characterization of Garvey’s testimony. Page 2 has edits and cross-outs. The May hearing separately records Roemer asking about aircraft-as-weapon reports. The draft characterization and the transcript establish different source observations. The four-page item 715 has a Garvey questions cover and handwritten prompts including after-action work, intelligence summaries and verbal briefings. The two scans supply topics and possible record types. Their preparation dates and authorship remain open. [Exact members and physical pages](SOURCE-PINS.json) · [May hearing transcript](https://www.9-11commission.gov/archive/hearing2/9-11Commission_Hearing_2003-05-22.htm)
+- **June 30 interview and July 1 meeting.** NYC Box 3 item 014 is a four-page member. Page 1 is headed `6/30/04 Interview with Jane Garvey`. Page 4 is headed `7/1/04 Family members meeting`. Keep the two headings and all four pages together as archived while indexing the events separately. The first three pages offer a later interview route and include handwritten references to the FAA Command Center and Twin Star on p. 3. The January testimony predates the dated June interview. [Exact member and page scope](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+## Verification and remaining records
+
+Verified 10 held source hashes, 28 fixed text anchors and 12 paired page renders and extracts. All five mirror members matched the archived size and CRC. The three handwritten files were visually inspected in full. Selected MFR page regions were visually inspected, with the threat paragraph, relative-threat statement and executive-summary passage read in the extracted layers. At the fixed render setting all 12 pairs have different pixels. Four page pairs have identical extracted text. Those counts describe the saved representations. The copies record the same October interview and count as one interview source. A filename, a marked classification label or an OCR difference alone leaves historical meaning and custody open. [Reproducible inputs, scope and results](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+The next discriminating records are the January supplement cover and Commission receipt or enclosure inventory, and the exact TSA or Commission copy of the classified Joint Inquiry response or cited rebuttal. An enclosure listing that matches a dated version would support a delivery link. A separate intake identifier or a listing limited to the written testimony would narrow that inference. For PD01–PD04, the separate corrected May 2003 QFR, recipient acknowledgment, signed FAA disposition, recommendation-specific response and applicable routing records remain open. [Earlier AWA-811 acquisition and item 77](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/eae18dcf1eeac4dc184a7101d68de9d49aa76b83/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-joint-inquiry-rebuttal-source-check-2026-11-09/README.md)
